      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FIGHTING FOR GOLD (4) was chasing a hat-trick of wins when finishing third by less than a length here 3 weeks ago. She slots into a superior gate this time and can get back to her winning ways. On top. MILES 'N' MILES (5) had a couple of starts in the winter and followed up a fresh third with a run prior to having a spell. He looked in good condition when winning a recent trial, and as long as the sting is out of the ground, he will once again be very competitive. SISTER ROYAL (6) is a lightly tried 5YO who resumed fresh up for another new trainer, and needed the run, finishing sixth in an 8-horse field here 3 weeks ago. She improves with racing and can get some of this at value. TUSKEGEE (2) is a consistent gelding holding his form this season, and he will find this easier than his last start fifth in BM76 company here 3 weeks ago over 1600m. Stick with him on an each-way basis. STONE COLD STUNNER (1) loves this trip and track and is always worth including in all combos.",
